%[text] # Plotting 3D Energyscape Info
%[text] The `plot3DEnergyscape` function shows a 3D acoustic image (range, azimuth and elevation) in 3D space. Every range bin of every direction is placed at its position relative to the sensor, and only the part within a dB window below the peak is shown. It can draw a point cloud, in which louder points are larger and more opaque, or nested semi-transparent isosurfaces at chosen dB levels.
%[text] This function is designed to work seamlessly with acoustic images generated by `clait.calculateAcousticImage()` for a set of directions that covers both azimuth and elevation, for example made with `clait.generateDirections()`.
%%
%[text] ## Namespace and Calling
%[text] The function is part of the CLAIT toolbox namespace and should be called using the full namespace qualifier:
clait.plot3DEnergyscape(imageData, structSensor, structImage, options)
%[text] ### Function Signatures
%[text] The function supports two calling modes:
%[text] #### Plotting Mode
[hPlot, hCbar] = clait.plot3DEnergyscape(imageData, structSensor, structImage, options)
%[text] #### Options Query Mode
opts = clait.plot3DEnergyscape('options')
%%
%[text] ## Input Parameters
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Parameter** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `imageData` | 2D double array | Yes | Acoustic image from CLAIT beamforming \[numRangeBins × numDirections\] |
%[text] | `structSensor` | struct | Yes | Sensor array configuration and signal characteristics |
%[text] | `structImage` | struct | Yes | Image formation parameters including the azimuth and elevation of each direction |
%[text] | `options` | struct | No | Visualization customization parameters (see detailed breakdown) |
%[text:table]
%[text]
%[text] ### **Detailed Breakdown of Input Structures**
%[text] #### 1. imageData
%[text] The 2D acoustic image matrix generated by `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`.
%[text] - **Dimensions**: `[numRangeBins × numDirections]`, one column per direction in `structImage`
%[text] - **Type**: Double array
%[text] - **Content**: Beamformed intensity values for each range and direction \
%[text] #### 2. structSensor
%[text] Structure containing sensor array setup and signal characteristics, you can use the same one as used for `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`. It is used to convert the image rows to ranges:
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Description** | **Units** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `sampleRate` | scalar | ADC sampling frequency | Hz |
%[text] | `numSamplesSensor` | scalar | Total number of samples in acquisition | samples |
%[text] | `speedOfSound` | scalar | Speed of sound in medium (default: 343) | m/s |
%[text:table]
%[text] ####
%[text] #### 3. structImage
%[text] Structure containing image formation parameters, you can use the same one as used for `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`:
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Description** | **Units** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `directionsAzimuth` | vector | Azimuth angle of each image column \[numDirections × 1\] | degrees |
%[text] | `directionsElevation` | vector | Elevation angle of each image column \[numDirections × 1\] | degrees |
%[text] | `decimationFactor` | scalar | Decimation factor applied to acoustic image (default: 10, as `calculateAcousticImage`) | dimensionless |
%[text:table]
%[text] The positions use the right-handed coordinate system of the toolbox with the sensor at the origin: X forward, Y to the left and Z up.
%[text] ####
%[text] #### 4. options (Optional)
%[text] Structure containing visualization parameters. Use `clait.plot3DEnergyscape('options')` to retrieve all available options with defaults.
%[text] **General Options:**
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `renderMode` | string | `'points'` | `'points'` = point cloud, `'isosurface'` = nested isosurfaces |
%[text] | `dbCut` | scalar | `-30` | Lower end of the dB window relative to the peak. Points below it are not shown and it is the bottom of the colorbar |
%[text] | `rangeLimits` | 1×2 vector | `[]` | `[minRange maxRange]` in m to only show part of the range, for example to hide the direct path at short range. `[]` = all |
%[text] | `normalizeToMax` | logical | `true` | Make the dB values relative to the peak |
%[text] | `colormap` | N×3 array | `parula(1024)` | Colormap matrix |
%[text] | `backgroundColor` | color spec | `'w'` | Background color |
%[text:table]
%[text]
%[text] **Point Cloud Options** (only used when `renderMode = 'points'`):
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `markerSize` | scalar | `20` | Marker size of the loudest points (points²), weaker points are smaller |
%[text] | `alphaRange` | 1×2 vector | `[0.05 0.9]` | Opacity from the weakest to the loudest points |
%[text] | `maxPoints` | scalar | `200000` | Maximum number of points, the loudest are kept |
%[text:table]
%[text]
%[text] **Isosurface Options** (only used when `renderMode = 'isosurface'`):
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `isoLevels` | vector | `[-6 -12 -20]` | dB levels of the surfaces relative to the peak |
%[text] | `isoAlphaRange` | 1×2 vector | `[0.2 0.9]` | Opacity from the lowest to the highest level |
%[text] | `voxelSize` | scalar | `[]` | Edge of the voxels the image is resampled on (m). Each voxel takes the maximum over the range bins it covers. `[]` = about 150 voxels over the largest side of the shown volume |
%[text] | `smoothing` | scalar | `3` | Box size of the 3D smoothing of the volume (odd, in voxels), `0` = off |
%[text:table]
%[text]
%[text] **Display and Labeling Options:**
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `showSensor` | logical | `true` | Mark the sensor at the origin |
%[text] | `showColorbar` | logical | `true` | Display colorbar |
%[text] | `colorbarLabel` | string | `'Relative Level (dB)'` | Colorbar label |
%[text] | `viewAngle` | 1×2 vector | `[-130 20]` | Camera azimuth and elevation, see `view` |
%[text] | `xlabel`, `ylabel`, `zlabel` | string | `'X (m)'`, `'Y (m)'`, `'Z (m)'` | Axis labels |
%[text] | `title` | string | `''` | Plot title |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] ## Output
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Output** | **Type** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `hPlot` | graphics handle | Handle to the scatter object (`'points'`) or an array of patch objects, one per level (`'isosurface'`) |
%[text] | `hCbar` | graphics handle | Handle to the colorbar object, or `[]` if colorbar is not shown |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] ## Examples
%[text] A full example is available, to quickly open it after installing the toolbox, run the following command:
clait.openClaitPlotting3DEnergyscapeExample
%[text] The general 3D imaging example combines all 3D functions of the toolbox:
clait.openClaitAcousticImage3DExample

